  "description": "Name and introduced-device rules (crates/peer intro.rs). A name is valid iff (1) no character anywhere in the untrimmed name is a control character (general category Cc: U+0000-001F, U+007F-009F) or one of U+061C, U+200B-200F, U+2028-202E, U+2060-2064, U+2066-2069, U+FEFF, and (2) after trimming Unicode White_Space from both ends it has 1..=maxChars Unicode scalar values (code points, not UTF-16 units). utf8Hex is the exact name. introDevices: check_intro_device(device) gives result (ok or a code); codes are checked in the order bad_id, bad_name, bad_kind, bad_key, bad_addr. bad_kind: kind phone iff os is ios / android (a hub may have no os; a phone must have one). The receiving node also refuses own_device / sender_device / duplicate, which depend on context and are not listed here.",
